export const dataLessons=[
 {name:'Data Sources',what:'The applications, files and devices where business information starts.',why:'Each system was built for a particular job, so it holds only part of a wider business story.',example:'ERP records revenue; CRM records customer activity; POS records store transactions.',need:'“The answer is in several systems.”',connect:'Source ownership and access come before connecting data. A source can contain structured tables or unstructured documents.',question:'Do all sources need to be replaced?',answer:'No. Start with the business question and identify which sources are needed. Integration can connect existing systems.'},
 {name:'Data Integration',what:'Making information from different sources usable together.',why:'A business question often crosses application boundaries.',example:'Link sales to the right customer and product across ERP, CRM and POS.',need:'“We export from three systems every time management asks.”',connect:'Integration brings information into a usable flow; preparation and agreed definitions make the combined information meaningful.',question:'Is integration the same as migration?',answer:'No. Integration connects data flows. Migration moves a system or dataset to a new place; the two can be part of the same project.'},
 {name:'Data Quality',what:'Checking whether data is suitable for the decision you want to make.',why:'Missing values, duplicates or inconsistent IDs can lead to misleading results.',example:'Check whether two rows represent one duplicated order or two real orders before removing either.',need:'“Two departments report different sales numbers.”',connect:'Quality checks belong throughout the flow, with owners and rules for resolving issues.',question:'Can a tool guarantee perfect data?',answer:'No. Rules, source processes and accountable owners matter. Measure the quality needed for the use case and keep evidence of changes.'},
 {name:'Data Transformation',what:'Changing the shape or representation of data so it can be compared and combined.',why:'Different systems can describe the same thing in different ways.',example:'Interpret 30/09/26 as 2026-09-30 using an agreed date convention; map SKU018 to the product master.',need:'“Our team keeps fixing columns and formats in Excel.”',connect:'ETL transforms before loading; ELT loads first and transforms afterward. Both need explicit rules and validation.',question:'Does transforming a value prove it is correct?',answer:'No. A consistent format can still contain an incorrect value. Transformation and quality checks work together.'},
 {name:'Data Warehouse / Data Platform',what:'A warehouse organizes business data for analysis. A broader data platform may also cover storage, processing, governance and access.',why:'Cross-system analysis needs reusable data structures rather than a new pile of exports each time.',example:'Analyze store, e-commerce and ERP sales together using agreed reporting definitions.',need:'“Our management report takes three days because we combine Excel files manually.”',connect:'Prepared data supports analytics and can feed AI use cases. A warehouse is not a replacement for every operational database.',question:'Do we need a warehouse, a lake or both?',answer:'Start with the uses and data types. A lake can retain varied raw data; a warehouse typically provides organized analytical data. Their capabilities can overlap.'},
 {name:'Analytics / BI',what:'Using data to understand what happened, investigate patterns and support a business decision.',why:'A pile of connected records still needs questions, definitions and interpretation.',example:'Compare sales by period and region, then investigate the category contributing most to a decline.',need:'“We have a dashboard, but a new question needs another export.”',connect:'BI often presents information through reports or dashboards; analysis can go further into relationships and explanations.',question:'Does a chart prove why something happened?',answer:'No. It can show a pattern or association. Test the explanation against additional evidence before concluding causation.'},
 {name:'Machine Learning',what:'Models that learn patterns from examples to make predictions or classifications.',why:'Some tasks need repeatable predictions rather than a fixed rule or a historical report.',example:'Estimate churn risk using a defined outcome, relevant historical features and validation data.',need:'“We want to predict which customers might leave.”',connect:'Models need relevant, governed data and evaluation. Their outputs can be combined with analytics and human decisions.',question:'Can we give customers an accurate churn score immediately?',answer:'Not responsibly without understanding the outcome, data and validation. A drop in purchases alone is a signal to investigate, not a validated prediction.'},
 {name:'Generative AI',what:'Models that produce content such as summaries, text or code from prompts and context.',why:'People may need help expressing a question or explaining and summarizing information.',example:'Draft a management summary using reviewed sales analysis and source context.',need:'“Management wants to ask business questions in natural language.”',connect:'Useful context, access controls and evidence matter. Generated language does not replace the underlying data work.',question:'Does AI know all of our business data?',answer:'No. It needs access to relevant context through an appropriate design. Check outputs against sources and state what is unknown.'},
 {name:'Streaming / Real-Time',what:'Processing data as events arrive instead of waiting for a scheduled group of records.',why:'Some business decisions become less useful when information arrives too late.',example:'Monitor incoming operational events when the required response cannot wait until tomorrow’s batch.',need:'“We need more current information for this decision.”',connect:'Batch and streaming are design choices within the same larger data flow. End-to-end freshness depends on every component.',question:'Can we call the whole system real-time?',answer:'Only if its actual latency and reliability meet the agreed requirement. Ask how fresh the data needs to be and why before proposing streaming.'},
 {name:'Data Governance',what:'The ownership, definitions, permissions and policies that make data usable responsibly.',why:'Teams need to know what a number means, where it came from and who may use it.',example:'Agree a revenue definition, record the source and mapping rules, and restrict sensitive customer fields.',need:'“Who owns this report, and who is allowed to see the data?”',connect:'Governance spans sources, preparation, the platform, analytics and AI. It is not a final checkbox.',question:'Does centralizing data make it automatically trustworthy?',answer:'No. Keep ownership, quality checks, lineage and access decisions explicit.'}
];
export const distinctions=[
 ['DATABASE vs DATA WAREHOUSE','An operational database supports day-to-day application records and transactions.','A data warehouse is designed to organize data for analysis across a business.','Ask: are we running the application, analyzing the business, or both?'],
 ['ETL / ELT','ETL: extract, transform, then load into the target.','ELT: extract, load, then transform using the target environment.','The key distinction is when and where preparation occurs. Neither removes the need for quality rules.'],
 ['BATCH vs STREAMING','Batch processes a group of records on a schedule or trigger.','Streaming processes incoming events continuously.','Ask how fresh the decision needs to be; avoid promising real-time without a defined architecture.'],
 ['DASHBOARD vs ANALYTICS','A dashboard presents selected measures in a repeatable view.','Analytics investigates questions and patterns; dashboards can be one way to present its results.','A dashboard can start a conversation without answering every follow-up question.'],
 ['ANALYTICS vs AI','Analytics uses data to examine and explain business patterns.','AI may predict, classify or generate content; it can support analysis but still needs evaluation.','Ask what decision the customer wants to improve, then choose the method.'],
 ['MACHINE LEARNING vs GENERATIVE AI','Predictive ML can estimate an outcome or assign a category from learned patterns.','Generative AI produces content. It is also based on machine learning.','A churn prediction and a written summary are different tasks with different evaluation needs.'],
 ['STRUCTURED vs UNSTRUCTURED DATA','Structured data follows a defined shape, such as transaction rows and columns.','Unstructured data includes documents, images and free text without the same fixed table structure.','Both may contain business value; their preparation and access patterns differ.'],
 ['DATA LAKE vs DATA WAREHOUSE','A lake commonly retains diverse data, including raw files, for multiple uses.','A warehouse commonly offers organized data for analytical queries and reporting.','Modern platforms can combine capabilities. Decide based on the workload, governance and consumers.'],
 ['INTEGRATION vs MIGRATION','Integration connects information or processes across systems.','Migration relocates data or a workload to another environment.','A customer may need one, the other, or both. Do not treat connecting reports as moving every application.']
];
